WEBVTT

NOTE Narration by an AI voice: Matilda (XrExE9yKIg1WjnnlVkGX), eleven_v4.

intro
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.420
Cursor CLI uses the Cisco Deep Time Series Model to catch a slowdown a fixed threshold missed.

ask
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.720
Checkout felt slow in Europe this morning, yet no alert fired.

why
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.640
Latency follows daily traffic, so a fixed threshold is either noisy or blind.

model
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.220
The model is pretrained, and runs on a container the team hosts in Azure.

connect
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.620
Cursor loads its Splunk skills and connects to the Splunk MCP Server.

find
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.680
It finds the checkout data, with its latency and region fields.

series
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.160
Then it builds a five-minute p95 latency series for every region.

baseline
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:48.980
Each series covers the full day, so the model sees the normal pattern first.

result
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:58.040
One anomaly, in EU West only. About two hours this morning, over four times the forecast.

chart
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.500
Splunk Web shows the same window, shaded red, far outside the forecast band.

ask-alert
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Next, the SRE asks for an alert that runs this check every 15 minutes.

draft
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.500
Cursor drafts a scheduled search with the same model call.

trigger
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.760
It fires on any anomaly in the last 30 minutes.

why-stop
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.000
Creating an alert is a write, so splunkctl waits for your approval.

create
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.440
Approved. Cursor reruns the same command, and the alert is created.

schedule
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.420
It runs every 15 minutes over the last day.

verify
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:43.380
A final splunkctl check confirms it's scheduled and enabled.

rhythm
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.520
The baseline follows the daily rhythm, so the next regional slowdown pages someone.

outro
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.920
From a vague complaint to a confirmed anomaly and a live alert, with one approval.
